A||||14||batboy||Honda vs. Fiero||||1
Z||000000||batboy||10-20-1999||10:41 PM||||When I bought my 85 GT I told myself, "NO RACING!" That's what my V8 Batmobile is supposed to be for. Well... today, a Honda CRX SI was driving like a bat out of hell, switching lanes, driving agressively, speeding, etc. I just had to put him in his place. I positioned myself next to him at the next set of lights and blipped the gas a couple of times. He did likewise.<P>The light turned green and we were off. The CRX immediately jumped out in front by half a car length. I chirped second gear and ran it up to 5 grand. The Honda stayed half a car length ahead and I'm thinking, "Oh guano! I'm going to lose!" I slam third and nailed it. Finally, I began slowly pulling even with him. I hit fourth and gained more ground. I had about one car length ahead of him when I noticed traffic ahead. I waved to him and hit the brakes and so did he.<P>That little close call was an eye opener. I didn't realize those little Hondas were that quick. I hated being behind, but sure was glad my car finally pulled ahead. That was one tough race. I'm going to be more careful with those Hondas next time. I also bent my aluminum clutch pedal all to hell in that incident. That'll teach me.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||10-20-1999||11:00 PM||||There's no way that CRX could keep up if it was stock.  I'm willing to bet that an '85 GT 4-speed will have no problem keeping up with or beating a stock CRX.  He must have done something to it under the hood <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  While I was at work some guy drove up in his newer Eclipse, the plates read something along the lines of "V8 blurr".  If that was a V8 then my V-6 would have to sound like a lawnmower.  It had to have been all stock.  Sounded like crap. We all got a good laugh. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||10-20-1999||11:13 PM||||Is the GT a 4speed or auto?  I am not busting on you here, but there should be no way that a crx should be able to get a better start than an '85 GT.  The GT has alot of torque.  What did the car look like?  Was it all riced up, or was it fairly stock looking?  I would be willing to bet that if it WAS stock looking, the guy probably put his money into the engine.  Those riceboys spend all their money on stickers, exhaust cans, and wings, so they have no money left over for performance.  Most of them just throw on a 4" exhaust tip and a k&n filter, and claim that they "moded" the car.  I can't wait to put some back in their places.||||reg||5
Z||000003||Shaun41178||10-21-1999||02:50 AM||||Man if you had reached 4th gear you must have been going at a pretty fast clip.  I know the 4 spd can hit 60 in 2 nd gear if taken to 6k.  But you said you shifted at 5 so I would think around 50 or so.  Seems to me like he beat you to 60.<P>Hey don't rag the CRX especially the Si's.  They were 16 second cars just like the Fiero was/is.  Sure it has a lot less torque but can rev much higher and has a flatter hp curve.<P>The CRX might have had a filter and maybe exhaust but I think that the CRX was relatively stock.<P>Eitehr way you pulled ahead so good kill!!  We need more stories like this on this board.  Perhaps not all from street racing but at the track as well.  I prefer the track over the street anytime but street is just awesome.<P>To add to the kill here I ran into a 3rd gen Camaro about a week ago and it said RS on the back bumper and it was a 5 spd so it was a 305 V8.  Went from a 15 mph roll and by 40 I already pulled a half car on the guy.  I was driving my auto like a stick and was manually shifting and really over revved it and I let off and switched gears and by this time the guy had pulled even with me but once I hit second and slammed the throttle I pulled another quick 1/2 car and kept it there up till about 70 or so.  I was just inching away from him but had to slow down for traffic.  He tried me again and again I shut him down.  not a very exciting race as i wasn't expecting him to win but he tried to jump me so I had to show him the power of the Fiero.  By the way I was juicing it.  If my bottle was warm I would've totally walked away from this guy but pressure was way down so the nitrous wasn't kicking right.  The 305 might have been modded but I didn't stop to talk to the guy.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||10-21-1999||07:54 AM||||Shiner, I have a 4 speed not an auto in my GT. The CRX SI I raced was stock looking, not "riced out." I admit that I didn't get a good jump off the line. I was babying it a little because I know I have a separated lower motor mount. Plus, I didn't realize he was that serious or that his car ran that good. Shaun, yes we were going way to fast for being on the street, which was stupid on my part. Probably twice the speed limit. You're right about this should be done at the track. **hanging my head in shame**||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||10-21-1999||02:07 PM||||I do a lot of city dashes with those cars, and clean them out pretty well... <BR>normally only 0-45 or 0-40 in a 35 zone.  My stock beat up looking (faded paint)85 SE humbles them quite a bit.  Normally though I get them right from the get go, then they pass me when I let off the gas.  I must admit  though they initiate all the dashes which is a sweeter victory in my eyes.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||10-21-1999||07:11 PM||||You guys should drive in Chicago.  On ogden the old route 66.  You can go 50 and its just mainly straight road until you see the lights turn red.  There are a lot of drivers that are jealous of you speeding and want to catch up, you might be going 70 and at the next stop light the _____ goes in the bus lane and cuts you off cause your thinking whose gonna go 70?  I obey the law when i drive except the speed, meaning turn signals and stuff.  Most people cheat if they are drag racing by moving foward past the pedestrian line giving the head start.  Whats sad is when i catch up to them and pass them.  Another thing is scary, not many cars are drag racing, ever see SUVs going in and out of traffic, or vans.  I hate these people and i do have things against suvs because who needs them in the city?  I like the story of the person posting, the SUV ran off the road while tailgating him. SUVs are just dangerous when people think they are sport cars and have 1.0G skidpad.  I like to hear more stories that people have about just driving with fieros and how they made the other drivers look bad or how someone avoided an accident.  Also people dont believe our fieros are the 2nd safest, yes i read the volvo is 1st place.  When you get in the fiero, yes its really low, and people think its plastic, all cars are created the same, fieros also have a frame, its built like a rollcage and the roof is stronger then most sheetmetal roofs.  Just my two cents please forgive me for my grammer.  English wasnt my fav subject.  but heres the anti suv site and read the hate mail the guy got.  <A HREF="http://poseur.4x4.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://poseur.4x4.org/</A>   im not against suvs well i am but i prefer monster trucks.  I like when people say well im up high and i feel so safe ya when they kill the person they hit cause their vehicle rolled over.<BR>   ||||reg||6
Z||000007||four50four||10-21-1999||09:17 PM||||must not get a whole lot of snow down there, because up here in the great white north. SUV's are great. you can cart your whole family around AND not get stuck while your at it. 4WD is great in the winter here, epecially, when you live out in the country like me, and the roads don't get plowed for sometimes for 2-3 days after a big storm. I do agree with you though, they are NOT race vehicles and should not be driven as sports cars.||||reg||3
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||10-21-1999||09:50 PM||||I agree, SUVs are nice, but not for racing or any kind of reckless driving at all! I saw at guy at my school flip his truck, and he was barely moving.. just pulled a corner too tight coming out of the student parking lot, and ended up on his side, on some guy's front lawn.. couldn't do that in a Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've been thinking about getting an SUV sometime, as a Fiero isn't the most practical car out there.. maybe an older chevy blazer or something.. fix it up, put in a stereo system.. not too sporty, but sorta fun to drive, and it'd be good in winter. (assuming it had 4WD)<P>wow, and to think this started out as a thread about racing hondas. hehe||||reg||1
Z||000009||lowCG||10-22-1999||01:08 AM||||Suvs are are a great laugh in the snow as well;they really don't stop any better than anything else,but usually go faster,get the picture...<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000010||batboy||10-22-1999||01:32 AM||||Winter storms in my part of Kansas are often a mix of ice and snow. I plod along at a slow speed in my ol' 4X4 Suburban. I get a laugh out of the fools who pass me with their yuppy SUVs, and then I have pull them out of the ditch or snowbank a couple more miles down the road. You're right about SUVs and 4X4s not stopping any better than other cars. On nasty days, I just get up earlier and allow more driving to work. Slow down when it's slick is good advice.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Pretender||10-22-1999||01:54 AM||||crx's are not slow, my best friend has one and before his motor swap(went to jap spec's) he was still ahead of me in the 1/4 mile. My car isn't stock but the auto-tranny is really killing me. the stock crx runs 15's i think and the fiero a 16? I'm not sure, but we do have them in the handling dept. Hondas have every part available to make them more then fast but we have to rely on smarts and MONEY to make these cars fast. T gave up on the 1/4 speed just because i hate losing. L8r.||||reg||10
Z||000012||DJRice||10-22-1999||08:58 AM||||Well I just bought a Jeep Grand Cherokee and I like it pretty well.  I have the best of both worlds now.  Im either on the ground in the Fiero or can see everything in the Jeep.  <BR>Buying the Jeep makes me appreciate driving my Fiero a bit more.  SUVs are awfully convienient for hauling your friends around or your stuff around, but I was a bit hesitant to buy one because every one has got one nowadays, and I kind of wanted something different.  I have actually left a grocery store and headed for the wrong Jeep.  But It rides and drives very nice.  <P>I think I may add nerf bars just so it will look different from all the other White G. Cherokees on the road.<P>Just my .04 (because that was a bit wordy for just .02)||||reg||10
Z||000013||ChadMan||10-22-1999||12:33 PM||||I love my Fieros, but eventually I'd like to have a smallish SUV (like a Cherokee or Blazer) - for a daily driver.  It would take Ohio's crappy pothole-lined roads much better than my Fieros, and I could actually see over a few people.<P>What kills me is how few people actually use SUVs for what they're good for - hauling lots of people around, towing trailers, going camping, and driving over obstacles like curbs and medians to get out of traffic jams.||||reg||1
Z||000014||HotFieroGT||10-22-1999||11:11 PM||||I'll have to agree with you guys on the misuse of SUV's.  Everyone in California has one, it seems to be a status thing.  I love watching those people park those tanks in the compact car spots, and we get so much snow here (hah!).  My 1972 Ford Bronco looks much cooler, gets better gas mileage, and does circles around those things offroad.  And best of all I have less than $3500.00 in it.<P>[This message has been edited by HotFieroGT (edited 10-22-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by HotFieroGT (edited 10-22-1999).]||||reg||6
